          "paragraphs": [
            "A PU-coated deck jacket in the pattern we've made since 1968. 300D polyester with a 0.35mm PU face, welded seams, no membrane to fail. Storm cuffs inside the sleeves, a hood that snaps off, and a back length that covers you bent over a rail.",
            "No breathability at all. It's a rubber coat. Work hard in it and you'll be wet from sweat instead of rain. For anything more than standing and hosing, look at the Salmon Bay Parka."
